  "content": {
    "title": "The Bachelorette Season 22 Premieres March 22, 2026: What to Expect",
    "text": "If you’ve been waiting for the next season of The Bachelorette, the premiere is finally just around the corner.Season 22 of The Bachelorette, starring The Secret Lives of Mormon Wives star Taylor Frankie Paul, premieres Sunday, March 22, 2026, at 8 p.m. ET/PT on ABC. Episodes will stream the next day on Hulu.The upcoming season marks a major change for the long-running franchise, which traditionally launches a new Bachelor or Bachelorette season in early January. This year, however, ABC shifted the schedule, pushing the premiere to March and moving the show to a brand-new night.Related: ‘The Bachelorette’ Season 22 Cast Revealed: ‘The Book of More-Men’ is Now OpenWhy ‘The Bachelorette’ Didn’t Premiere in JanuaryFor years, Bachelor Nation fans could count on a new season arriving the first Monday of January. That didn’t happen in 2026 for two main reasons.First, ABC and ESPN hold the broadcast rights to the College Football Playoff, including the national championship game, which aired Monday, Jan. 19. Rather than compete with one of the biggest sports broadcasts of the year, the network appears to have delayed the franchise’s return.Second, ABC reorganized its reality-TV schedule.Related: All the Taylor Frankie Paul ‘Bachelorette’ Spoilers — Including Who Made the Final 3Instead of airing The Bachelorette on Mondays, the network shifted the show to Sunday nights beginning this spring.The move opened Mondays for American Idol, which premiered Jan. 26 and now anchors the network’s Monday lineup. Meanwhile, NBC’s rival singing competition The Voice returned Feb. 23.In other words, ABC was positioning American Idol directly against The Voice while giving The Bachelorette a fresh night of its own.Related:‘Bachelorette’ Taylor Frankie Paul Deletes Steamy IG Story—Fans Are Convinced They Know Who’s in ItWho Is the New Bachelorette?Season 22 features a notable departure for the franchise: the lead comes from outside Bachelor Nation.Taylor Frankie Paul is best known as a breakout star of the Hulu reality series The Secret Lives of Mormon Wives. The Utah-based influencer rose to internet fame during the “MomTok” viral saga and has built a massive TikTok following with her candid storytelling about relationships, motherhood and personal growth.According to ABC, the 31-year-old single mom is hoping to leave headline-making drama behind and focus on finding lasting love.Related:‘Bachelor’ Fan-Faves Back For New HGTV ‘Bachelor Mansion Takeover’ Competition SeriesThe Men Competing for Taylor’s Final RoseABC has revealed the 22 men who will compete for Paul’s heart this season.The group includes a wide range of careers and personalities, from a cowboy entrepreneur and ocean lifeguard to a former professional baseball player and a three-time Paralympian.Among the contestants are:Aaron, 32, a product manager from UtahBrad, 29, a cowboy from CaliforniaDoug, 28, an ocean lifeguard from San DiegoJohnnie, 30, a former pro baseball playerTrenten, 35, a professional athlete and ParalympianYou can see the full list of contestants and their bios here.Related:‘Dancing With the Stars’ Welcoming ‘The Bachelorette’ For an ‘Insane’ Group DateWhen Does ‘The Bachelorette’ Air Each Week?Once the season premieres, new episodes of The Bachelorette will air Sundays at 8 p.m. ET/PT on ABC and stream the next day on Hulu.With a brand-new lead, a new night and a fresh group of suitors, this season could look very different from past installments of the reality dating franchise.🌹 SIGN UP for our The Bachelor newsletter to stay up to date on the latest Bachelor Nation news, exclusive interviews, episode recaps & more 🌹This story was originally published by Parade on Mar 15, 2026, where it first appeared in the TV section. Add Parade as a Preferred Source by clicking here.",
